.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-NETBOOT-SERVER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-netboot-server
.Nd install or clone the machines of a rack over the network, offline, from an installed kldload machine or its USB stick
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm serve
.Nm
.Cm arm-install
.Ar mac | Cm any
.Ar answers
.Op Fl -netdev Ar mac2
.Nm
.Cm arm-all
.Ar dir
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Nm
.Cm arm-deploy
.Ar mac
.Fl -golden Ar name
.Fl -disk Ar disk
.Op Fl -hostname Ar name
.Op Fl -netdev Ar mac2
.Nm
.Cm golden
.Ar dataset
.Op Cm as Ar name
.Nm
.Cm disarm Ar mac | Cm disarm-all
.Nm
.Cm never
.Op Cm list | Cm add Ar mac Op Ar note ... | Cm remove Ar mac
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the kernel, initramfs and root image this machine was installed
from \(em kept at install time with
.Ev KLDLOAD_KEEP_NETBOOT Ns =1 ,
or read from the live USB stick it booted from \(em to other machines on
the LAN, with the offline package mirrors inside, so a rack installs with
no internet.
.Cm serve ,
run by
.Pa kldload-netboot.service ,
writes an HTTP tree, an
.Xr nginx 8
configuration with directory listing off, and a
.Xr dnsmasq 8
configuration for proxy DHCP and TFTP on one interface, and runs both.
Proxy DHCP answers network boot requests beside the network's own DHCP
server and gives out no addresses.
.Pp
Nothing is installed unless it is armed.
Every machine that network-boots from here gets
.Pa boot.ipxe ,
which looks for
.Pa armed/ Ns Ar mac Ns Pa .ipxe
for each of its network interfaces in turn and runs the first it finds.
A machine with none falls through to its own boot order.
Arming writes that file:
.Cm arm-install
to install from the answers file, and
.Cm arm-deploy
to receive a golden as a ZFS stream over the same HTTP server, so a clone
needs no ssh key.
An armed install first shows a summary of what will be installed and
counts down; a key opens a menu to change the profile, distribution and
options, and a password the answers lack is asked for on the machine's
own screen, never sent on the command line.
.Pp
Machines listed in
.Pa /etc/kldload/netboot-never
are never installed from here:
.Cm arm-install
and
.Cm arm-deploy
refuse them, and
.Pa boot.ipxe
sends a machine with any listed interface back to its own boot order,
open mode included.
A line in that file that does not parse stops the server rather than
dropping the protection.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm serve
Run the server.
.It Cm arm-install Ar mac answers
The next network boot of
.Ar mac
installs, from the answers file.
With
.Cm any
in place of a MAC, every machine that network-boots gets the menu: a key
installs, the countdown boots its own disk.
.It Cm arm-all Ar dir
Arm every
.Ar mac Ns Pa .env
in
.Ar dir ,
refusing duplicate MACs or host names; exit 1 unless all were armed.
.Fl -dry-run
checks without arming.
.It Cm arm-deploy Ar mac Fl -golden Ar name Fl -disk Ar disk
The next network boot of
.Ar mac
writes the golden
.Ar name
to
.Ar disk .
.It Fl -netdev Ar mac2
.Ar mac
starts the boot and
.Ar mac2
carries the download: for a fast card that cannot network-boot under
UEFI.
.Cm arm-install
also reads
.Ev KLDLOAD_NETBOOT_NETDEV
from the answers file; the option wins.
.It Cm golden Ar dataset Op Cm as Ar name
Stage a dataset as a golden stream.
.It Cm disarm Ar mac , Cm disarm-all
Remove the token; the machine boots locally.
.It Cm never Cm list
The never list.
.It Cm never Cm add Ar mac Op Ar note ...
Add a machine, disarm it if armed, and rewrite
.Pa boot.ipxe
now.
.It Cm never Cm remove Ar mac
Take it off.
.It Cm status Op Fl -json
The payload \(em followed by its
.Pa VERSION
file as written by the build, which
.Pa tests/estate-sweep.sh
reads the build commit from \(em whether the service is running, the
goldens and the armed machines.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Read from
.Pa /etc/kldload/netboot.env
by the service and by every command run by hand; a variable already set
wins.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NETBOOT_PORT
The HTTP port; default 8080.
.It Ev NETBOOT_IFACE
The interface to serve on; default the one with the default route.
.It Ev NETBOOT_MENU_TIMEOUT
Seconds the summary counts down; default 10, and 0 for no menu.
.It Ev NETBOOT_DISTROS
The distributions the menu offers; default
.Ql fedora .
.It Ev NETBOOT_PAYLOAD_NET , Ev NETBOOT_NET_DISTROS
A second, smaller payload without the offline mirrors, used for the
distributions named (default
.Ql rhel arch )
only when it is the same build as the main one.
.It Ev NETBOOT_PAYLOAD , Ev NETBOOT_NEVER
The payload directory and the never list.
.El
.Pp
.Ev NETBOOT_MENU_TIMEOUT
and
.Ev NETBOOT_DISTROS
are read when arming: re-arm to change them for an armed machine.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload-netboot/
The retained payload.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/netboot-serve/
What is served:
.Pa boot.ipxe ,
.Pa armed/ ,
.Pa answers/ ,
.Pa golden/
and
.Pa ipxe/ .
.It Pa /etc/kldload/netboot-never
One MAC a line, with a note.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 when a step failed, named; 2 on a usage error.
