.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dnsmasq 8 ,
.Xr kldload-restore-machine 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-11 a lab machine network-booted from its second card, which
is why
.Pa boot.ipxe
tries every interface; the same day the payload written at install went
under a dataset's mount point and vanished at the next boot.
On 2026-09-13 a command run by hand ignored
.Pa netboot.env
and reported a different payload from the one being served.
The never list came on 2026-09-29, for a machine that must not be
installed over.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Pa answers/
holds each answers file as written, passwords included, and is served
without authentication to anyone on the LAN who knows the MAC; listing is
off, and
.Cm arm-install
warns.
.Pp
The iPXE image is not signed: a machine with Secure Boot on refuses it.
x86 only.
The site's DHCP server must not also hand out a boot server and file.
